 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? It depends how fluent you are already. If you speak one fluently as an adult, the other usually comes next. They share many common words and spelling is usually similar. The big challenge is hearing the difference in pronunciation. It is. So whichever one you want travel to is the one to start with. Then start listening to news in the other language too. That will help your ear a lot. They' both big TV markets, so plenty. The Netherlands leads for shows you can watch without language skills, though. Then go for it. Whichever one you start with now, you can always switch later if you change your mind.",
